---
/**
 * The one auth affordance on public pages: "Log in", or "Log out" once the
 * reader has a session.
 *
 * Public pages are prerendered — one HTML file served to everyone — so this
 * cannot be decided on the server. Both links are always in the markup and CSS
 * shows exactly one of them, keyed off a `data-signed-in` attribute that
 * `CustomHead.astro` sets on `<html>` before the first paint. Nothing is
 * fetched and nothing swaps in after load, so there is no flash of the wrong
 * button.
 *
 * The attribute comes from a readable, content-free hint cookie
 * (`SIGNED_IN_HINT_COOKIE`). It grants nothing: forge it and you get a header
 * that lies to you, while every private URL still goes through the guard. That
 * is the trade this makes deliberately — a cosmetic lie the reader tells
 * themselves, in exchange for no flash and no per-page request.
 *
 * "Log in" points at `/private/`, not at the SSO endpoint. The guard is what
 * knows where sign-in lives and what to come back to; sending readers straight
 * at `DOCS_SSO_URL` would skip the `state` nonce and the `returnTo` it stores.
 *
 * Rendered only when `showAuthControls` is on — see `src/config/sidebar.mjs`.
 */
---

<div class="auth-control print:hidden">
	<a class="auth-in" href="/private/">Log in</a>
	<a class="auth-out" href="/auth/logout">Log out</a>
</div>

<style>
	.auth-control {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.auth-control a {
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		text-decoration: none;
		white-space: nowrap;
		padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
		line-height: 1;
	}

	.auth-control a:hover {
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
		background-color: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
	}

	/* Signed out is the default, because it is the state a reader with no
	 * cookies is in and the state a forged cookie cannot fake into something
	 * more permissive. */
	.auth-out {
		display: none;
	}

	:global(html[data-signed-in]) .auth-in {
		display: none;
	}

	:global(html[data-signed-in]) .auth-out {
		display: inline-block;
	}
</style>
